/target
/.env
/tests/ui/node_modules
/tests/ui/package-lock.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
/.skein/

# macOS Finder droppings. `src/.DS_Store` was tracked from 2026-06-30 to SKEIN-520.
.DS_Store

# `.claude` in a working checkout is a symlink into the owner's live store — another repository's
# data, mounted here for the agent's benefit. It is not this repository's and must never be
# committed from it.
/.claude

# `kit::ensure_store` scaffolds a store wherever it is pointed, and a `git add -A` from the repo
# root once swept a whole scaffold into an unrelated commit (582d017 — `settings.json` and 28 files
# under `skein/`, every one of them a copy of `src/probe/` or `src/store/` or generated by
# `probes::ensure_probe_in`). Ignoring the scaffold's own names at the ROOT ONLY means the next
# accidental scaffold is invisible to `git add` instead of one flag away from being committed. The
# canonical copies live in `src/store/` and `src/probe/`; nothing is meant to be at the root.
/skein/
/settings.json
/handoffs/
/hook-log/
/hooks/
/journals/
/mailbox/
/memory/
/sessions/
/shared-home/
/shared-rw/
/skills/
/status/
/tasks/
/telemetry/
